flowchart LR
    ROOT["FullProject/"]:::root
    ROOT --> DOCS["docs/<br/><i>the permanent memory</i>"]:::docs
    ROOT --> CFG["config/<br/><b>the entire insurance domain pack</b><br/>intents - skills - dids - menus"]:::cfg
    ROOT --> SRC["src/readycall/"]:::src
    ROOT --> MOCK["mock/bank_core/<br/>fixtures + 2000-customer generator"]:::misc
    ROOT --> SCR["scripts/<br/>run_scenario - gen_diagrams"]:::misc
    ROOT --> TST["tests/<br/>unit - contracts - scenarios"]:::misc
    ROOT --> INF["infra/<br/>docker-compose + schema SQL"]:::misc

    SRC --> D1["domain/<br/><b>no I/O at all</b>"]:::layer
    SRC --> D2["ports/<br/><b>Protocols only</b>"]:::layer
    SRC --> D3["adapters/<br/><b>no business rules</b>"]:::layer
    SRC --> D4["services/<br/><b>imports only domain + ports</b>"]:::layer
    SRC --> D5["entrypoints/<br/>the runnable processes"]:::layer

    RULE["<b>the dependency rule, in one line:</b><br/>domain knows nothing - ports know domain -<br/>services know domain and ports - adapters know<br/>ports and a vendor. <b>Any file that breaks that is a bug.</b>"]:::key

    CFGN["<b>why config/ is separate and large.</b> Every insurance<br/>literal lives there, so retargeting this to a hospital<br/>line or a telco desk means swapping YAML, not touching<br/>services/. That reuse claim is D28, and it is enforced:<br/>no insurance literal may be hardcoded in services/."]:::note

